@rekram1-node with the fallback to deriving cost from messages present in the memory (from commit affc11a), migration is not strictly required in a sense that it will break the functionality but for older sessions the cost reporting will still be bugged.

from my local testing the migration was fine but again I don't know the extent of how many sessions people have, it could be a concern.

as @maharshi365 mentioned I can also add lazy migration, that only runs when a session is loaded, checks if the session has cost field, and run the migration if needed. I am currently not aware if users can manually run migrations in OC or not, also if it's fine from maintainers perspective to only updated new sessions I am fine with that as well, let me know @rekram1-node .

```suggestion
rm -rf ${OPENCODE_CACHE_DIR:-${HOME}/.cache/opencode}
```

The parameter `elt` is already typed as `Element` in the function signature, so the `instanceof Element` check will always be true for valid calls. However, the comment mentions that WebView2 can call this with non-elements, which suggests the type constraint isn't being respected at runtime. Consider typing the parameter as `any` or `unknown` to accurately reflect the runtime behavior this workaround is addressing.
```suggestion
  window.getComputedStyle = ((elt: unknown, pseudoElt?: string | null) => {
    if (!(elt instanceof Element)) {
      // WebView2 can call into Floating UI with non-elements; fall back to a safe element.
      return originalGetComputedStyle(document.documentElement, pseudoElt ?? undefined)
    }
    return originalGetComputedStyle(elt as Element, pseudoElt ?? undefined)
```

The localStorage access on line 25 could throw an error in environments where localStorage is not available (e.g., SSR, certain browser configurations). Consider wrapping this in a try-catch block or adding a check for localStorage availability.
```suggestion
  const getInitialLanguage = (): Language => {
    if (typeof window === "undefined" || typeof window.localStorage === "undefined") {
      return "en"
    }
    try {
      const stored = window.localStorage.getItem("opencode-language") as Language | null
      return stored ?? "en"
    } catch {
      return "en"
    }
  }

  const [language, setLanguage] = createSignal<Language>(getInitialLanguage())

  function setLanguageWithStorage(lang: Language) {
    setLanguage(lang)
    if (typeof window !== "undefined" && typeof window.localStorage !== "undefined") {
      try {
        window.localStorage.setItem("opencode-language", lang)
      } catch {
        // Ignore storage errors; language is still updated in memory
      }
    }
```
